Source: pgedge-snowflake
Section: database
Priority: optional
Maintainer: pgEdge Build Team <support@pgedge.com>
Build-Depends:
 debhelper-compat (= 13),
 pgedge-postgresql-all <!nocheck>,
 pgedge-postgresql-server-dev-PG_MAJOR_VERSION,
 pgedge-postgresql-server-dev-all,
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://github.com/pgEdge/snowflake

Package: pgedge-postgresql-PG_MAJOR_VERSION-snowflake
Architecture: any
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 pgedge-postgresql-PG_MAJOR_VERSION,
 ${shlibs:Depends},
Conflicts:
 postgresql-PG_MAJOR_VERSION-snowflake,
Provides:
 postgresql-PG_MAJOR_VERSION-snowflake,
Replaces:
 postgresql-PG_MAJOR_VERSION-snowflake,
Breaks:
 postgresql-PG_MAJOR_VERSION-snowflake,
Description: Snowflake is a PostgreSQL extension providing an int8 and sequence
 based unique ID solution to optionally replace the PostgreSQL built-in
 bigserial data type.
